<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela sees 96 oil exports at 2.727 mbpd - source.</title>
<headline>Venezuela sees 96 oil exports at 2.727 mbpd - source.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela expects to earn nearly $17 billion in oil revenues in 1996 from average daily exports of 2.727 million barrels of crude oil and products, according to recent calculations by state oil company Petroleos de Venezuela (PdVSA), which were obtained by Reuters from sources at the Ministry of Energy and Mines.</p>
<p>The revenues will translate into a $8.552 billion contribution to the treasury, which compares to $6.640 billion in 1995, according to PdVSA's revised revenue projections for the year.</p>
</text>
